(LiNC syntax-check fixture: block faults, ten of them)
(Every fault below is one block's own mistake, so all ten are marked at once.)
(Use it to see the red gutter bars, the word underlines and the n/10 counter.)
(Ctrl+PageDown walks to the next fault, Ctrl+PageUp to the previous one.)
(Do not run this file: the load gate refuses it, which is the point.)
O3001
G21 G90 G54 G17 G40 G49 G80
G0 X-120 Y-120 Z10
(1 comment nesting: the inner pair is not allowed, the interpreter refuses it)
G0 X-110 Y-120 (outer (inner) tail)
(2 an unclosed comment takes the rest of the line)
G0 X-100 Y-120 (no closing bracket
(3 a word with no value: the F has nothing to apply)
G1 X F300
(4 the same letter twice in one block)
G1 X-90 X-80 F300
(5 a G number out of range)
G123 X-70
(6 an M number out of range)
M1234
(7 a negative feed)
G1 X-60 F-100
(8 the N word numbers the block only at its start)
X-50 N100 G1 F200
(9 an unbalanced bracket in an expression)
G0 Z[#1+2
(10 an assignment with no value)
#2001 =
G0 Z10
